== Problem

+ Run `just docs build` and open the site root at a desktop and a phone width, in light and dark.
+ 🔴 "Here's a real task." sits above an `mt ls` table, not a task. The lede wraps at 40rem. The "typeset · rendered" card fills a whole screen.
+ 🔴 The header shows a "GitHub" text link beside an icon, and the theme toggle's glyph sits off center in its box.
+ 🔴 The sidebar's "Model" group holds one page, Concepts.


== TO-BE

- 🟢 The site root says "Here's a real task.", shows the task file, then how `mt ls` lists it. The typeset card is one sentence with a collapsed preview.
- 🟢 The lede uses the hero's width.
- 🟢 The header shows the GitHub mark and a small sun/moon switch, centered, keyboard-operable, announced as a switch.
- 🟢 The title button reads "Copy page as Markdown".
- 🟢 Concepts sits in the Start group, and no Model group remains, in the sidebar, llms.txt and README's index.


== Source of truth

- `www/utils/site.typ`: `NAV`, which the sidebar, llms.txt and README's documentation index read.
- `docs/src/readme.typ`: README's order, intro line then task.


== Changes

- `www/utils/ui.typ`: reorder the hero's faces and fold the typeset card into a `<details>`.
- `www/utils/demo.typ`: the `mt ls` lead-in and the typeset sentence.
- `www/templates/layout.typ`: the GitHub icon link and the theme switch.
- `www/utils/site.typ`: the Copy page as Markdown label, and Concepts moved into Start.
- `www/assets/styles/main.css`, `www/assets/styles/components.css`: the header icons, the switch, the lede and the smaller card.
- `README.md`: regenerated by `just docs md`.


== Out of scope

- Other pages' content. This touches the header, the sidebar groups and the site root only.
- The mobile sidebar layout, which lists every group above the content.


== Dogfood

Not applicable. The change is the docs site's look.
